// Allowlist.pkl — schema ONLY. No data lives here.
//
// The allowlist is the named sets the permits refer to: which symbols
// may be bought, how much may be spent in one run, and how long the
// rolling window is. The values live in config/policies/allowlist.pkl.

// The properties are declared on the MODULE (not inside a class):
// the policy file `amends` this module and fills these in. A `class
// Allowlist` wrapper used to hold them, which made the module itself
// have none of them — real `pkl eval` failed, and the failure was
// invisible until the Docker build first ran pkl, because the JSON
// was hand-written and the check skips when pkl is absent. Do not
// reintroduce the class wrapper.

// Symbols the script may buy. Checked in Rust against
// OrderLeg.instrument.symbol. Everything else is denied.
symbols: Listing<String>(length >= 1, isDistinct)

// Per-run dollar cap. Enforced in Rust as
// quantity * live quote price <= maxDollarsPerRun.
maxDollarsPerRun: Int(this > 0)

// Rolling window, in days. A second buy of the same symbol for the
// same account inside this window is a 409 and is not forwarded.
// NOTE: the window definition is NOT decided yet — this field is
// the shape of the decision, not the decision.
rollingWindowDays: Int(this > 0)
